Dear Theo, Ben &nbsp;Please see attached an updated folder of relevant correspondence, now including two letters sent out by PG this afternoon. &nbsp;Kind regardsJess&nbsp;​​​​Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateFrom: Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt; Sent: 29 September 2025 17:17To: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; B.Williams@4newsquare.comCc: Martyn Day &lt;mday@leighday.co.uk&gt;; MJacques@leighday.co.uk; Nichola Marshall &lt;nmarshall@leighday.co.uk&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Subject to CIP - Nox Emissions - PG Draft WS&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Dear allSorry – additionally it is important that Alicia’s statement expressly sets out the position taken by PG in correspondence re: Gramercy, namely that &nbsp;Gramercy has no control over the day-to-day management or decision making of PG or its parent company;&nbsp;Neither does Gramercy have any role in the conduct, control or management of these proceedings.&nbsp;Theo&nbsp;&nbsp;Theo&nbsp;Barclay​​​​BarristerDirect&nbsp;+442078222100&nbsp;Mobile&nbsp;+447411&nbsp;731074&nbsp;Chambers&nbsp;+442078222000&nbsp;4&nbsp;New&nbsp;Square&nbsp;Chambers​Lincoln's&nbsp;Inn,&nbsp;London&nbsp;WC2A&nbsp;3RJFollow&nbsp;us&nbsp;on&nbsp;YouTube&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedIn​Discover&nbsp;our&nbsp;Events&nbsp;Privilege and Confidentiality Notice:This email is private as between the sender and the intended recipient. The information contained in this message and any file that may be attached to it are confidential between those parties and may be privileged. Any other party who receives it in error is not permitted to read, use, copy, discuss or pass on the information contained in either the message or its attachments, nor are they entitled to take any action in reliance on the contents. Therefore, if you are not the intended recipient you are kindly requested to contact me immediately by telephone on the numbers given above.Members of 4 New Square Chambers are regulated by the Bar Standards Board.NOTE TO SOLICITORS: ALL PAPERS RECEIVED FOR MEMBERS OF CHAMBERS WILL BE SENT FOR SECURE SHREDDING&nbsp;UPON COMPLETION OF WORK&nbsp;UNLESS YOU SPECIFICALLY REQUEST THEIR RETURN.From: Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;Date: Monday, 29 September 2025 at 16:58To: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Benjamin Williams KC &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc: Martyn Day &lt;mday@leighday.co.uk&gt;, MJacques@leighday.co.uk &lt;MJacques@leighday.co.uk&gt;, Nichola Marshall &lt;nmarshall@leighday.co.uk&gt;, Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Subject to CIP - Nox Emissions - PG Draft WSDear Jessica&nbsp;I have been preparing written submissions for the PTR on the PG management issues. With that in mind, I’ve got a few points on the draft WS.&nbsp;Witness statement&nbsp;There are a number of areas where it would be helpful for Alicia to provide some more information in this statement. I understand the sensitivities surrounding these areas, but in circumstances where the court is very likely to ask these questions, it is far better to have something in a witness statement rather than have to give an answer on instructions in court.&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; First, we need to provide the court with some more detail of the further funding provided by Gramercy, including, importantly, the difference between the 14 Aug 2025 $65m tranche (I understand to be used for overheads generally) and the 19 Sept 2025 $30m tranche (ringfenced for Pan NOx). It is important that Alicia explains in her statement that the $30m is so ringfenced, and ideally how that has been achieved.&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Second, given Martyn’s statement about the PG case leads resigning, &nbsp;Section IV [14.4] of Alicia’s WS needs fleshing out. At present I find this para a little hard to follow. Ideally Alicia needs to explain when the case leads resigned, why they did, and when their notice period ends (and if this is after the conclusion of the evidence in the PDD trial).&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Third, it is very likely that Ben or one of the other KCs will be asked at the PTR about the circumstances of Peter’s resignation, what precisely he has alleged and why it is wrong. I understand you will be limited in what you can say, but if you can go further than what is in the WS, it would be a good idea to do so. At the very least Alicia needs to state what has already been said in correspondence: that there is a dispute with Peter.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; I look forward to seeing the next draft.&nbsp;CROs&nbsp;On a separate point, on the steps that need to be taken re: CROs and letters sent under the CROs to confirm removal/addition, is there any reason that the relevant steps can’t be done immediately (i.e. before we put in submissions for the PTR)? If those steps can be taken now, they should be.&nbsp;All best,&nbsp;TheoFrom: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Monday, 29 September 2025 at 13:43To: Benjamin Williams KC &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;, Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc: Martyn Day &lt;mday@leighday.co.uk&gt;, MJacques@leighday.co.uk &lt;MJacques@leighday.co.uk&gt;, Nichola Marshall &lt;nmarshall@leighday.co.uk&gt;, Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogus