TE until you’ve got it sorted.&nbsp;I wouldn’t use the phrase “would be meritless and designed to distract from the substantive proceedings” in para 3. That is putting it too high. The Ds expectation of security is legitimate. Our point is they are sufficiently secured. To say the proposed application is ‘meritless’ is not a great idea when we know we are about to get additional ATE. I think you should say “would fail” instead.&nbsp;I cannot work out what the reference to Willers v Joyce was supposed to be to. I agree the now-referenced case doesn’t look on point either. I suggest leaving out this paragraph and asking whoever drafted the original letter whether they meant a different case.&nbsp;I would delete para 8 because we know that this isn’t going to bring matters to a close!&nbsp;Theo&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Theo&nbsp;Barclay​​​​BarristerDirect&nbsp;+442078222100&nbsp;Mobile&nbsp;+447411&nbsp;731074&nbsp;Chambers&nbsp;+442078222000&nbsp;4&nbsp;New&nbsp;Square&nbsp;Chambers​Lincoln's&nbsp;Inn,&nbsp;London&nbsp;WC2A&nbsp;3RJFollow&nbsp;us&nbsp;on&nbsp;YouTube&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedIn​Discover&nbsp;our&nbsp;Events&nbsp;Privilege and Confidentiality Notice:This email is private as between the sender and the intended recipient. The information contained in this message and any file that may be attached to it are confidential between those parties and may be privileged. Any other party who receives it in error is not permitted to read, use, copy, discuss or pass on the information contained in either the message or its attachments, nor are they entitled to take any action in reliance on the contents. Therefore, if you are not the intended recipient you are kindly requested to contact me immediately by telephone on the numbers given above.Members of 4 New Square Chambers are regulated by the Bar Standards Board.NOTE TO SOLICITORS: ALL PAPERS RECEIVED FOR MEMBERS OF CHAMBERS WILL BE SENT FOR SECURE SHREDDING&nbsp;UPON COMPLETION OF WORK&nbsp;UNLESS YOU SPECIFICALLY 