%VW2 Porsche6,959,6757,141,252181,57700%Vauxhall1,909,2492,000,00090,75100%Volvo1,674,5055,000,0003,325,49500%Mazda2,688,2812,685,173-3,1083,1080%Toyota3,422,3242,951,874-470,450470,45016%Total94,433,49883,708,383-10,725,11515,400,80318%&nbsp;This would provide sufficient indemnity to cover the claimant’s cost exposure to 31 July 2026, as per the assumptions outlined in Anna’s email (Increasing the T3 trial prep assumption to 50% would add £1.4m total LOI to the above).&nbsp;The brokers have indicated that they are able to provide a quote for some of the required topup by the end of the week, exact amounts per manufacturer will be provided tomorrow. &nbsp;It is not clear on the timing or certainty of availability of the remainder of the topup as the brokers have to approach the open market. I expect to have an update on this position tomorrow also. &nbsp;Tom&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Tom&nbsp;CrowGroup&nbsp;Financial&nbsp;Controller+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;708From: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 22 October 2025 20:31To: T.Barclay@4newsquare.com; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.comCc: B.Williams@4newsquare.com; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;Hi Theo&nbsp;See below a break down of the additional cover that is being sought - this aligns with the approach Leigh Day is taking. I don't yet have pro rated cover per defendant: @Tom Crow&nbsp;is that something you could assist with please?&nbsp;60% of the Defendants incurred costs (including those from CMH1 and CMH2, the costs of cost budgeting from both CMH1 and CMH2, and the Non-Tranche 3 Quantum costs).100% of the Defendants Tranche 2 (£90.5 million) and First General approved future costs (£19.25 million)Defendants Tranche 3 approved future costs up to 31 July 2026, broken down as follows:100% of CMC, Selection of Sample Claimants, Individual Statements of Case, Disclosure, Witness Statements, and PTR71% of the Tranche 3 Co-Ordination Costs (12.5 out of 17.5 months)Trial Preparation: We had been considering seeking between 33% and 50%. However, Leigh Day is seeking 50%, and we consider a more conservative approach is appropriate in light of the scrutiny. If we go with 50% this would add c. £1.5 million LOI which we can accommodate in the budget. &nbsp;Defendants Second General approved future costs up to 31 July 2026, broken down as follows:44% of GLO Management CostsFortnightly Meetings to September 2026 at 67%T3 Expert Reports/2G ADR: Figures based on Claimant offers. 100% of £10.2m for expert reports, and 44% of £1.8m for ADR. Leigh Day have based their approach on agreed figures, with the following exceptions: &nbsp;where not agreed, Defendants counteroffer, and where no counteroffer, Claimants offer).&nbsp;BestAnna​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;Sent: Wednesday, October 22, 2025 8:08 PMTo: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc: B.Williams@4newsquare.com &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2 &nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Hi Anna&nbsp;&nbsp;Can you let me know how much further ate cover you are planning to get and what the total pro rated cover per defendant solicitors firm is anticipated to be? That makes &nbsp;a&nbsp;difference, I think, to whether we should say more. If we anticipate getting very close to eliminating the shortfalls, then I would be more in favour of sayin