Dear Board,


&nbsp;


In follow up to my email at 12.52 today, I am writing to ask for immediate attention to be given to addressing my (and the other case leaves) employment position
 to the Defendants, Court, clients and any other relevant stake holders.


&nbsp;


As Signature's draft application points out at 8(b)(iii) - a letter was sent out yesterday, naming me as the PG contact.&nbsp;


&nbsp;


That I am named as the contact appears to have been an administrative oversight, and I put no blame on the sender of the letter, however this has now lead
 to a misleading position, or what will be a mislead position if not immediately clarified, underpinning the concerns I had regarding paragraph 27 of the letter sent to the Defendants on Tuesday 23 September (see my email at 12.52 today and my suggestion at
 15.59 on 23 September).&nbsp;


&nbsp;


The SRA Code of Conduct at 1.4 says &quot;You do not mislead or attempt to mislead your
clients,
 the court&nbsp;or
 others, either by your own acts or omissions or allowing or being complicit in the acts or omissions of others (including your
client)&quot;


&nbsp;


By this letter having gone out, and by repeat correspondence continuing to go out in my name on the Ford and Volvo litigations, and the names of the other
 case leads, without appropriate context that we are working our notice, I have real concerns that the firm is (and I am) in breach of 1.4 of the code of conduct. This applies not only to correspondence to the Defendant firms, but also to clients and any external
 parties.


&nbsp;


This requires immediate attention, especially in respect of my position.&nbsp;


&nbsp;


SL have asked for a response by 4pm. Without wanting to force the hands of the board, I must be insistent that the below (or clarification of that nature)
 is sent before that deadline to clarify the position:


