 Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our Privacy Policy.From:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;james.burke2@wtwco.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;03 October 2025 3:33 PMTo:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Emissions Case Leads &lt;EmissionsCaseLeads@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Pan NOx Notification&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Thanks Michael. This is with insurers. We have asked them to get back to us asap given the PTR on Monday.&nbsp;We will be in touch with their response.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;James Burke&nbsp;Associate Director (Solicitor)Litigation and Contingent Risk FINEX Global&nbsp;WTWOn behalf of Willis Limited, 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ (registered number 181116)On behalf of Willis Towers Watson SA/NV, Quai des Vennes, 4020, Liège, Belgium (registered as a branch in the UK at 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ UK Branch Number BR021056) in relation to all EEA-regulated business&nbsp;D: +44 (0)20 31248037M: +44 (0)7831 162591&nbsp;james.burke2@wtwco.comwww.wtwco.com&nbsp;Financial, Professional, and Executive Risks (FINEX)Your Trusted Partner in Managing Complex Risk: Expertly navigating Litigation Risk, Cyber, Directors &amp; Officers, Financial Institutions, Mergers &amp; Acquisitions, Professional Indemnity, and Operational Risks within WTW.Part of our wider risk solutions capabilities at WTW&nbsp;At WTW we work flexibly - whilst you may receive emails from me out of working hours, I do not expect a response or action outside your own working hours.&nbsp;&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;03 October 2025 12:20To:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;james.burke2@wtwco.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jonathan Simon &lt;jonathan.simon@wtwco.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Emissions Case Leads &lt;EmissionsCaseLeads@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Fw: Pan NOx Notification&nbsp;Hi James,&nbsp;Good to speak to you yesterday. As discussed, these applications were launched, and then heard, on an incredibly compressed timescale, at a time when there were i) a number of competing other critical path deadlines and ii) significant managerial changes and upheaval within PG. We apologise that the insurers were not put on notice sooner. On a positive note, and as per the attached, Counsel have advised that they do not feel that prospects of success have been materially altered as a result of these applications.&nbsp;&nbsp;To confirm, we need to try and reach agreement with the Defendants on these costs today&nbsp;to avoid them being aired at the PTR on Monday.&nbsp;In terms of the timetable for when these applications were made to when judgement was handed down:&nbsp;Defendants raised concerns over the content of the reports of Dr Heitz at the PTR on 29 July;Defendants crystallised those concerns in correspondences on 8 August;Claimants replied with detailed responses on 20 August;Applications were made by the Defendants (without response to our 20 August letter) on 27 August;Witness evidence for the applications was filed 2 September;Skeletons were filed 8 SeptemberHearing 10 September and oral judgement handed down 11 September.&nbsp;&nbsp;The timeframe for these applications also overlapped with finalisation of the supplemental expert reports and the substantive PDD Trial skeleton. We have since been provided with cost schedules by the Defendants for us to consider them with the schedules still being updated even to date. The costs sought by the Defendants are as set out in the below table, with 