 Day &lt;mday@leighday.co.uk&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Fiona Huddleston &lt;FHuddleston@leighday.co.uk&gt;; Jamie Macfarlane &lt;jmacfarlane@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Counsel CFAs &nbsp;Hi Sophia&nbsp;Thank you. This is a crucial document - not least because of the cost sharing provisions. I understand George and Sarah were due to discuss. I certainly have not had an opportunity to consider with the requisite detail. I also understand that many of the firms have not executed the Agency Agreement so the inter-play between those documents and the CFA cannot simply be assumed. As such I would rather we hold off sending this. I'm hoping to speak to George today.&nbsp;&nbsp;@Martyn Day&nbsp;re quantum counsel - I note you intend to instruct them in LD's name - is that correct? Could we arrange a time to discuss this please?&nbsp; There will be all manner of aspects this feeds into and worth discussing.&nbsp;BestAnna&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From:&nbsp;Sophia Thomson &lt;SThomson@leighday.co.uk&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Friday, October 10, 2025 9:51 AMTo:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Martyn Day &lt;mday@leighday.co.uk&gt;; Fiona Huddleston &lt;FHuddleston@leighday.co.uk&gt;; Jamie Macfarlane &lt;jmacfarlane@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Counsel CFAs&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;&nbsp;Hi Anna &amp; Michael,&nbsp;With apologies for a follow up so soon in such a busy time, I would be grateful if you could let me know by 11.30 if this draft is approved.&nbsp;This is just so that I can get something out to the clerks and allow them to come back with any questions today before George drafts the remainder this weekend.&nbsp;Best,Sophia&nbsp;Sophia&nbsp;Thomson​​​​Costs Executive0161&nbsp;938&nbsp;0575​leighday.co.ukFollow&nbsp;us&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Panagram, 27 Goswell Road, London, EC1M 7AJ&nbsp;&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Sophia ThomsonSent:&nbsp;09 October 2025 17:35To:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Martyn Day &lt;mday@leighday.co.uk&gt;; Fiona Huddleston &lt;FHuddleston@leighday.co.uk&gt;; 'Jamie Macfarlane' &lt;jmacfarlane@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Counsel CFAs&nbsp;Hi Anna, Michael&nbsp;Please see attached an example GLO specific counsel CFA as drafted by George McDonald.&nbsp;We have had a few rumblings from counsel that they want these all signed this week ahead of the PDD trial.&nbsp;There were a few outstanding points, so I had a brief conversation with George just now to resolve these.&nbsp;In summary:&nbsp;Paragraph 10: George noted the potential for disparity between this and how clients are defined in the GLOs. He noted that, as long as all clients on the Group Register are represented by firms who have, or will shortly have, entered into a corresponding Agency Agreement, this should be fine. His concern was if there are clients represented by firms who will not be entering into the AA. I told him that not all firms have signed but that they will eventually be party to the AAs.Paragraph 15: This needs to reflect to cost sharing provisions in each GLO and will therefore need to be amended on the basis of each.&nbsp;George suggested that, to appease counsel and to allow him to finalise the remaining CFAs due to the nuance of paragraph 15, we should circulate the attached draft version with the clerks this week (i.e., tomorrow). He said we should state that the only change will be paragraph 15, and it will be similar, if not the same, terms, but that we still need to check and redraft where necessary. The redrafting will be done by George over the weekend so we should be able to tell them we will have final versions for all GLOs early next week.&nbsp;Circulating this draft will be done in the hopes that getting something out – and also allowing for an opportunity to provide comments – will give us the breathing room needed to this final point checked over the weekend.&nbsp;It is our intention to circulate this draft tomorrow morning.&nbsp;Please could you let us know if you are happy with this so that we can do so?&nbsp;Separately, Zoe O’Sullivan KC and Jennifer Meech at Serle Court have not yet been sent the Pan NOx CFA and we will circulate that to them tomorrow morning too, however we are just noting for completeness that LD will be the only signatory to this.&nbsp;We look forward to hearing from you.&nbsp;Best,Sophia&nbsp;Sophia&nbsp;Thomson​​​​Costs Executive0161&nbsp;938&nbsp;0575​leighday.co.ukFollow&nbsp;us&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Panagram, 27 Goswell Road, London, EC1M 7AJ&nbsp;&nbsp;We are committed to protecting your privacy when you use our services and treat all personal data in accordance with our Privacy PolicyDisclaimerThe information contained in this communication from sthomson@leighday.co.uk sent at 2025-10-10 09:52:08 is confidential and may be legally privileged. It is intended solely for use by those authorised to receive it. If you are not so authorised, you are hereby notified that any disclosure, copying, distribution or taking action in reliance upon the contents of this information is strictly prohibited and may be unlawful. We do not accept service of documents by email.Please note that we only provide our bank account details in a password protected PDF. The password will be communicated separately by telephone. We will never send changes