Responses are being reviewed for 2 and 3, in the meantime please see below for 1:
&nbsp;
1. The original LOI approach on 30 September 2025 as was:
&nbsp;
1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 50% of the Defendants’ claimed incurred costs (including Non T3 Quantum costs);
2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 50% of the Defendants’ claimed cost of cost budgeting;&nbsp;
3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 100% of all approved costs to 31 July 2026 (excluding the Tranche 3 PTR, Trial Preparation and Trial phases future approved costs); and
4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 0% of all non-approved pending phase costs (Tranche 3 Expert Reports phase and Second General ADR Settlement phase).
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
The updated LOI approach now adopted (based on Cost Counsel advice to be cautious) is:
&nbsp;
1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 60% of the Defendants’ claimed incurred costs (including Non T3 Quantum costs);
2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 60% of the Defendants’ claimed cost of cost budgeting;&nbsp;
3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 100% of all approved costs to 31 July 2026 (including Tranche 3 PTR phase in full, 50% of Trial Preparation&nbsp; phase but still excluding Trial phase future approved costs); and
4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 100% of all offered non-approved pending costs for Tranche 3 Expert Reports phase and Second General ADR Settlement phase.
&nbsp;
We decided to calculate the adverse costs exposure to 31 July 2026 rather than to the conclusion of the budgeted period (December 2026). This is informed by the indication given by Cockerill J on Day 2 of the July PDD PTR that the parties
 should expect the PDD Judgment to be handed down by July 2026.
&nbsp;
These percentages of how much work would be incurred by July 2026 are applied not only to the pre-existing Tranche 2 (PDD Trial) and First General cost budgets but also to the Tranche 3 (Quantum Trial) and Second General cost budgets. The
 calculations exclude the Defendants' costs contained within the Tranche 1 KBA cost budget, as they were unsuccessful in that trial.
&nbsp;
A further assumption applied is that, in the absence of Court-approved budgeted amounts for certain phases, specifically, Tranche 3 Expert Reports and Second General ADR/Settlement Discussions, the Claimants’ offered figures have been adopted
 on the basis that these constitute a reasonable estimate of the amounts likely to be approved. Approval of these phases to take place after the January 2026 CMC.
&nbsp;
Proceeding on the assumption that Judgment in the PDD Trial will be handed down by July 2026 and given that the Tranche 2 PDD and Tranche 3 Quantum cost budgets run concurrently up to that date, it is expected that work relating to the
 forthcoming Quantum Trial will need to be undertaken irrespective of the outcome.
&nbsp;
By 31 July 2026, all work undertaken pursuant to Tranche 2 and the First General Costs Budget will have been fully incurred, as the relevant budgeted period runs from June 2024 to April 2026, concluding with the completion of the Spring
 PDD Trial. In respect of the Tranche 3 and the Second General Costs Budgets it has been necessary to assess the adverse costs exposure by reference to the anticipated progress within each phase as at that date.
&nbsp;
By 31 July 2026, work would have been fully concluded by the Parties in all of the following phases:
&nbsp;
·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tranche 3 CMC
·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tranche 3 Selection of the Sample Claimants
·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tranche 3 Individual Statements of Case
·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tranche 3 Disclosure
·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tranche 3 Witness Statements
·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tranche 3 Expert Reports
·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tranche 3 PTR
&nbsp;
At this point, Tranche 3 Co-Ordination Costs will remain outstanding for the working phases. Applying a pro-rata apportionment, 12 months of the 17-month budgeted period will have elapsed, representing approximately 71% of the budget for
 that phase incurred pre-31 July 2026.
&nbsp;
The only other phases that will not, at least in part, have concluded by 31 July 2026 are the Tranche 3 Quantum Trial Preparation and Tranche 3 Quantum Trial phases. However, it is foreseeable that the parties will begin to incur costs
 in respect of counsel’s brief fees for the Quantum Trial from at least Spring 2026 onwards. On that basis, we have adopted the conservative assumption that approximately 50% of this Tranche 3 Quantum Trial Preparation phase will also have been incurred at
 this point.
&nbsp;
Similarly, in relation to the Second General Costs Budget, which spans the period April 2026 to December 2026, a comparable pro-rata analysis indicates that, as of 31 July 2026, approximately 44% of the approved costs will have been incurred
 in the following&nbsp; phases:
&nbsp;
·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Second General GLO Management Costs (or Pan-NOx Litigation Management Costs)
·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Second General ADR/Settlement Discussions (not approved yet but LOI based on what the Claimants have offered)
&nbsp;
