gs are paying’: 1.6m claimants head to high court as carmakers finally face punishment for Dieselgate | Motoring | The Guardian.&nbsp; Two Leigh Day partners are quoted at length.&nbsp; There is a Sunday Times article planned, and I imagine that the FT will write about it too (they have published a few good pieces on the case).&nbsp; We have been contacted by AfP - the comms team is aware of this - and a host of media online about the trial.&nbsp;None of this coverage even mentions our firm, and we don't even have a LinkedIn post about it.&nbsp; Could we please fix this by Monday?&nbsp; Assuming that we have a press release on this, I would start by replying to Adam Vaughan at the Times, below, and AfP who wrote a week or two ago.&nbsp; I have written previously about how the French press is particularly important to the case.&nbsp; Please then reach out to the Guardian, the FT, and any other broadsheets that we have contacts with.&nbsp;Matt​​​​Matt&nbsp;Hunt(He/Him)Legal&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;697From:&nbsp;Priscilla Mendes &lt;pmendes@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Friday, October 10, 2025 17:26To:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Broomberg, Jaime &lt;Jaime.Broomberg@fticonsulting.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Dunford, Kit &lt;Kit.Dunford@fticonsulting.com&gt;; Strat Comm Pogust Goodhead &lt;pogustgoodhead@fticonsulting.com&gt;; Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Paula Razera &lt;prazera@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Dougie Inglis &lt;dInglis@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: The Times / dieselgate trial start&nbsp;Thanks, @Broomberg, Jaime.Shall I also ask your team to copy me in all responses to the press, please?&nbsp;On Anna’s point – is FTI preparing a PR about PG staying as lead solicitor?&nbsp;Best,Pri&nbsp;Priscilla Mendes (she/her)​​​​ (shChief External Affairs and Strategy Officer+ 44 0 7493 014 571m Men&nbsp;From: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;D