@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Paula Razera &lt;prazera@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Dougie Inglis &lt;dInglis@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: The Times / dieselgate trial start&nbsp;You don't often get email from jaime.broomberg@fticonsulting.com. Learn why this is importantCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;&nbsp;Hi Pri,&nbsp;Hope all is well.&nbsp;Your team should continue to lead on standard media enquiries relating to the trial – responding to requests about the timeline, providing background information etc – as you are all much closer to the litigation than us. We were involved directly this week on the PTR as the hearing related more broadly to the firm’s reputation and the broader issues we have been managing.&nbsp;However, Kit and I are happy to provide further support wherever necessary when the trial begins. We would like to ask that you and your team please copy us in on all media enquiries as there will likely be requests that touch on both the trial and PG’s role. It will be helpful for us to keep track of the inbound and advise where necessary. Of course we won’t respond to any requests without discussing it with you first.&nbsp;Kind regards,Jaime&nbsp;Jaime BroombergSenior Director, Crisis TeamStrategic Communications&nbsp;FTI Consultingjaime.broomberg@fticonsulting.com+44 7974 042600&nbsp;200 Aldersgate |&nbsp;Aldersgate Street&nbsp;London, EC1A 4HDwww.fticonsulting.com&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Priscilla Mendes &lt;pmendes@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Friday, October 10, 2025 3:47:24 PMTo:&nbsp;Dunford, Kit &lt;kit.dunford@fticonsulting.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Paula Razera &lt;prazera@pogustgoodhead.com&g