Thank you for circulating.&nbsp; We have accepted all changes save the last.&nbsp; Saying that Anna will be available to assist is unnecessary (as she is a partner in PG working on the case – it
 therefore just states the obvious), and it dilutes the message and opens space for defendants to try to create mischief at a time when the law is volatile due to
Mazur.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
It has however a matter of some dismay that we still have no agency agreement.&nbsp; Theo and I have seen the latest version via Leigh Day.&nbsp; While the change to the agreement itself concerning
 PG retaining supervision on its staff is understandable, the proposed change to the side letter is obviously unacceptable.&nbsp; It would indicate that PG continues to make decisions about who works on the common issues in a manner which is inconsistent with its
 resignation as lead, and undermines everything that the arrangement is intended to achieve.&nbsp; It is also impossible to justify such a significant gloss on the agency agreement being included in a so-called side letter which we do not intend to disclose.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
I told the judge yesterday that agreement was imminent.&nbsp; That was because I was told before the hearing that the only point remaining with the agreement was PG’s desire to remove reference
 to LD “solely” directing matters etc, and I had already advised LD that I was content for “solely” to be removed.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
It needs to be understood: (i) that the attached note must be filed today; but (ii) if at the point it is filed we still have no agency arrangement in agreed form, then Theo and I will
 have to tell the court that the information we gave it yesterday was wrong, and that the agency agreement remains unfinalised.&nbsp; That would be extremely unfortunate, and would inevitably provoke further disruptive intervention from defendants (who note, at
 the moment appear not to be demanding to see the agency agreement).&nbsp; &nbsp;
&nbsp;
Theo and I would therefore strongly encourage you to get the agency agreement finalised today, and to undo the unacceptable change to the side letter.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Kind regards
&nbsp;
Ben













